=== ARTICLE: The AnatomyBuilder ===
[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-anatomy@497c254d44fa1fc28df6db8fe1fb50269bb6e963/docs/img/pipeline.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]The AnatomyBuilder[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Built on your PC.[/b] Redistributing CBBE or BodyTalk needs their authors' permission, so only Nahka's own work ships, as a patch applied to YOUR CBBE: 0 CBBE or BodyTalk files in the download.
[*][b]Finds the game anywhere[/b] (Steam, GOG, MO2), reads every skin texture format, and writes across drives under MO2.
[*][b]New in 1.2.0:[/b] a 3BBB stage and a men's stage.
[*][b]AnatomyRebuild[/b] puts the outfit and neck fixes on your own BodySlide builds.
[*][b]Download:[/b] [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-anatomy/releases/tag/v1.2.0]GitHub, v1.2.0[/url]. VirusTotal 0/75: [url=https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f93eb0dd1abcd53dc2fbfc08922eaa63291483b17260dae812d9d2024b30bf7e]AnatomyBuilder.exe[/url], [url=https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/eebf55daaf3edbdea266c40aa543c2127a02eecd88821600a61fd453aa463051]AnatomyRebuild.exe[/url].
[/list]

=== ARTICLE: Compatibility and settings ===
[size=4][b]Compatibility and settings[/b][/size]

[b]Needs:[/b] Anatomy Engine 1.2.0, F4SE, Runtime Database, CBBE 2.7.2 with its BodySlide files, BodySlide. Install with Vortex or MO2; manual installs are not supported.
[b]Optional:[/b] AAF, Rapport, LooksMenu, MCM, BodyTalk 4 with its BodySlide files (for M-M), 3BBB with Skeletal Adjustments for CBBE, any physics preset (Anatomy brings its own).

[b]With AAF alone:[/b] aim, the mouth and lips, the sex body sounds, arousal from scenes, tube collision, stretch and toys, M-M.
[b]With Rapport too:[/b] moans, face expressions, glances, brows by depth, and the sound switch in its MCM.
[b]Without AAF:[/b] the genitals, the physics, nudity arousal and skirt physics still work.

[b]Upgrading from 1.1.1:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install Anatomy Engine 1.2.0, then Anatomy 1.2.0, over the old ones.
[*]Run AnatomyBuilder 1.2.0 again.
[*]In BodySlide, rebuild "Anatomy Body"; for men, build "Anatomy Male Body" (or "... Uncut") instead of BodyTalk4.
[/list]
Existing saves carry on.

[b]Settings:[/b] Anatomy's MCM has one page (Arousal, 9 controls). The engine reads its ocbp.ini; Rapport's MCM drives its knobs, the sound switch included.
